<article class="env-lemma" id="09HN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09HN">Lemma <span data-tag="09HN">9.15.2</span>.</a> Let $K/E/F$ be a tower of algebraic field extensions. If $K$ is normal over $F$, then $K$ is normal over $E$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\alpha \in K$. Let $P$ be the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $ over $F$. Let $Q$ be the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $ over $E$. Then $Q$ divides $P$ in the polynomial ring $E[x]$, say $P = QR$. Hence, if $P$ splits completely over $K$, then so does $Q$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>